ompany also provides OpenWrap, a header bidding solution; Connect, a solution that provides additional data and insights to publishers and buyers; Activate, which allows buyers to execute direct deals on its platform across publisher inventory; Convert, a commerce media solution; and Identity Hub, an ID management tool for publishers that leverages specialized technology infrastructure to simplify alternative identifier marketplace. Its platform supports an array of ad formats and digital device types, including mobile app, mobile web, desktop, display, video, over the top video, connected television, and media. The company was incorporated in 2006 and is based in Redwood City, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Rajeev K. Goel | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $275K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $65K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $37K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["PubMatic, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $945M market cap on $283M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -8.0pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 65% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $67M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -8.0pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 138% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3836691032269566},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PubMatic (NASDAQ:PUBM) Price Target Raised to $25.00","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/pubmatic-nasdaqpubm-price-target-raised-to-25-00.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794556606.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Why PubMatic (PUBM) shares are sliding today","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nasdaq/pubm/news/why-up-down/why-pubmatic-pubm-shares-are-sliding-today-3","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794336347.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What to expect from PubMatic\u2019s (PUBM) Q3 earnings","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/expect-pubmatic-pubm-q3-earnings-170136079.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794330096.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"PubMatic (PUBM) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/pubmatic-pubm-q3-2026-earnings-071621000.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794295774.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"PubMatic forecasts Q4 revenue of $91M-$93M while raising full-year CapEx to $24M-$28M (NASDAQ:PUBM)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4669490-pubmatic-forecasts-q4-revenue-of-91m-93m-while-raising-full-year-capex-to-24m-28m","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794288818.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"PUBM Q3 20